# Valgrind suppressions for poc's conservative garbage collector.
#
# GarbageCollectedHeap.Collect scans every word of the machine stack for
# things that look like heap pointers (poc's rtl/llvm/GarbageCollectedHeap.Mod:
# each word goes to MarkCandidate), including words that were never
# written. Memcheck reports each such read as an uninitialised-value error:
# TestLiveness and TestStreams, which force collections, showed 20 and 24
# of them, all "Conditional jump or move" with MarkCandidate as the top
# frame (confirmed live, 2026-10-03). That is how a conservative collector
# works, not a bug in the binding.
#
# Only uninitialised-value errors whose TOP frame is MarkCandidate are
# suppressed; the same kinds of error anywhere else, and every invalid
# read/write and leak, are still reported.

{
   poc-gc-markcandidate-cond
   Memcheck:Cond
   fun:GarbageCollectedHeap.MarkCandidate
}
{
   poc-gc-markcandidate-value8
   Memcheck:Value8
   fun:GarbageCollectedHeap.MarkCandidate
}
